  "$comment": "What the MIPS32 and MIPS64 sheets show that LLVM's Mips TableGen and the unofficial Sail do not carry: sections, groups, formats, descriptions, pseudocode, register names, pseudo-instructions, in the decoder's order. Rows of instructions only MIPS64 has (LLVM's HasMips3 / HasMips64 / IsGP64bit) are left out of MIPS32. tools/isa/gen-mips.mjs merges them into src/isa/generated/mips{32,64}.mjs. A row's extension overrides the ISA level LLVM's predicates give (RDHWR, EHB, JALR.HB are Release 2, SSNOP MIPS32, PREF MIPS IV). constraints and distinct are the operand values the manual calls UNPREDICTABLE (a link instruction reading $ra, JALR with rd = rs).",
